   "gap": "Reconstruct, with explicit model, sampling and regularity scope for each estimate and theorem (no maximization treated as a complete inferential guarantee, no hidden regularity), the selected Fisher 1922 estimation arguments the handbook route does not yet contain: (a) Section 9 location and scaling beyond the Cauchy and Type III forms: the Type IV centre of location and the Type VII/IV location and scaling efficiencies of moments (pp. 340-341); (b) Section 10, the efficiency of the method of moments for the Pearsonian curves generally, with the Type VII/II tables and the 80 per cent region (pp. 342-355); (c) Section 11, the reason for moment efficiency near the normal curve (pp. 355-356); (d) Section 12(1), Poisson series estimation and information (pp. 357-359), and Section 12(3), the dilution-series estimate and its efficiency (pp. 363-366); (e) for the grouped normal data of Section 12(2) (pp. 359-363): existence and limiting law of the grouped maximum likelihood estimate under stated regularity, a quantitative fixed-phase periodic-remainder bound for grouped information, and sampling calibration of the goodness-of-fit discrepancy (L / chi-square), which fisher-grouping-and-moments.tex lines 207-219 and 350-363 state are not established; (f) the Type III large-p expansions of sigma_p and n', the 80 per cent threshold (pp. 335-337) and the end-point-governed location regime -1<p<=1 (p. 337), which the owned body lines 586-590 and 614-618 state are not reconstructed.",
